  "term": "muscle relaxant",
  "definition": "A muscle relaxant is a drug used in surgical anesthesia to reduce muscle activity. In the supplied source, pancuronium is an example that inhibits muscle-type nicotinic acetylcholine receptors, which blocks the signaling that activates muscle.",
